# README markdown tables

`known_mei_polymorphism_id` (and similar fields) can contain literal `|`
(e.g. `g1k:…|lr:…`). That **splits markdown columns** and shifts the row.

## Required

- When refreshing the gold example table in `README.md`, run
  `scripts/update_readme_example_table.py` (do not hand-edit table rows from
  raw TSV).
- Every cell must go through `retro_miner.readme_example_table.markdown_table_cell`
  (pipes → `;`, newlines → space).
- After writing, `assert_markdown_table_shape()` must pass (header cell count
  equals every data row).

## Do not

- Paste TSV / support / polymorphism IDs into README table cells without
  escaping `|`.
- "Fix" one shifted row by hand without regenerating via the script.
